# PortfolioDB scheduled jobs, run by supercronic in the `scheduler` service.
#
# Times are in the container's TZ (PORTFOLIODB_TZ, default UTC). Every job is
# safe to run more often than needed:
#
#   * snapshot_prices.py exits immediately outside the configured market window
#     (app/market_window.py — set it from the Settings page), so the every-5-
#     minutes tick below does not need to know the window. Change the window in
#     one place, not here.
#   * advisor.py brief and fd_weekly_enrichment.py no-op or degrade cleanly
#     without their API keys, so an install without keys logs and moves on.
#
# Working directory is /app/app so the bare imports resolve the way they do on
# a host; supercronic logs each run's output to the container's stdout.

# Price snapshots — every 5 minutes; the Python guard decides whether to work.
*/5 * * * *   cd /app/app && python snapshot_prices.py

# Market overview benchmarks (index futures, volatility) — every 15 minutes,
# round the clock on weekdays plus Sunday evening, because that is when futures
# trade and the whole point of collecting them is the hours your own market is
# shut. Deliberately NOT gated by the market window, and it records no row in
# snapshot_runs, so Data Health and the MCP cutoff keep meaning "the portfolio's
# prices" — see the comment in snapshot_prices.main.
*/15 * * * 0-5   cd /app/app && python snapshot_prices.py --benchmarks

# Daily advisor brief, 07:00 on weekdays.
0 7 * * 1-5   cd /app/app && python advisor.py brief --kind morning

# Weekly fundamentals enrichment, Saturday 06:00 (cache-first, cheap).
0 6 * * 6     cd /app/app && python fd_weekly_enrichment.py --profile weekly
